    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mohnton’s post office started as Mohn’s Store in 1857 and kept that name until 1906, when it was renamed Mohnton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohnton%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "An 1887 Reading Eagle article warned that without a railroad, Mohnton would have to haul over 6,000 tons of coal to Reading at a cost exceeding $20,000 a year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mohntonpa.com/history/index.html",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wyomissing Creek cuts through Mohnton, once powering mills that evolved from gunsmithing to hat making to hosiery production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mohntonpa.com/history/index.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Globe Hat Factory, the fourth hat plant built in Mohnton, still stands opposite the lower depot on Main Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mohntonpa.com/history/index.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mohnton was incorporated as a borough in 1907 after a long tradition of milling, gun‑making, and wool hat manufacturing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://mohntonboro.org/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Bohler’s three‑story cigar factory, established in the late 19th century, employed 60 workers and helped fuel Mohnton’s industrial growth.",
